    ],
    "sci:doi": "10.7916/tw5k-ys98",
    "sci:citation": "Dataset citation: Center for Integrated Earth System Information (CIESIN), Columbia University. 2025. GRID3 NGA - Travel Time Friction Surface v1.0. New York: Columbia University. https://doi.org/10.7916/tw5k-ys98. Accessed",
    "ciesin:category": "Infrastructure",
    "ciesin:tags": "GRID3",
    "ciesin:sedac_doi": "10.7916/tw5k-ys98",
    "ciesin:purpose": "The aim of this work is to generate two friction surfaces for modeling physical accessibility: one incorporating walking speed only, and another combining walking and motorized travel speeds. Motorized speeds are applied exclusively on roads that are present and passable by vehicles; in all other areas, walking speeds are used.",
